guide.academic_exams.title: Academic Exams
guide.admission.p1: An admission track is one concrete way to enter the same university.
guide.admission.p2: Requirements are minimum thresholds. For safer planning, also compare yourself with typical admitted scores.
guide.admission.p3: Mode any means one language proof is enough. Mode all means every listed proof is required.
guide.admission.p4: Scholarships and aid can noticeably reduce total cost, so always check track details.
guide.admission.title: How to read admission tracks
guide.exam_basics.p1: Admissions usually need two parts: academic scores and proof of language proficiency.
guide.exam_basics.p2: Requirements differ by country and university, so check each track directly.
guide.exam_basics.p3: Language requirements are especially important for international programs.
guide.exam_basics.p4: Simple strategy: first cover minimums, then improve scores for stronger options.
