guide.title: How UniSearch works in simple words
guide.unichance.p1: {chance} shows an approximate admission chance. It is guidance, not a guarantee.
guide.unichance.p2: The estimate is based on your data: scores, language, budget, and selected track requirements.
guide.unichance.p3: Easy reading: 80-100 high, 60-79 good, 40-59 medium, below 40 low.
guide.unichance.p4: Check Best Track to see where your chance is strongest inside that university.
guide.unichance.title: {chance} (estimated admission chance 0-100)
guide.unifit.p1: {fit} builds a university list for you. It uses your filters, budget, preferred locations, and profile data.
guide.unifit.p2: If exam or language data is missing, you still see options, but we mark that extra proof may be needed.
guide.unifit.p3: One university can have several admission tracks. We check each track separately, so your best option may be inside a lower-ranked university.
guide.unifit.p4: When you update profile data, the order updates too. This is expected: results always reflect your current information.
